# Template for `<config home>/env` -- by default ~/.config/skuggi/env.
#
#     cp .env.example ~/.config/skuggi/env && chmod 600 ~/.config/skuggi/env
#
# This is the one file skuggi reads credentials from, and the reason it exists is
# that `skuggi` is a command you run from any directory: there is no project root
# to hang a .env on. Keys here reach every invocation without going in your shell
# rc. `skuggi-doctor` warns if the file is group- or world-readable.
#
# The repo's own `.env` is NOT loaded -- only this file, and only from the config
# home. App config (providers, models, paths, graph bounds) belongs in
# `<config home>/config.json` instead; edit it with the `config` verb.
#
# Precedence, highest first:
#   shell environment  >  this file  >  config.json  >  built-in defaults
#
# Spelling matches the environment exactly: settings take the SKUGGI_ prefix,
# vendor credentials do not.

# --- secrets (never stored in config.json) ---
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...
# OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...
# The openai/chatgpt providers can also read ~/.codex/auth.json (codex login),
# which is already an absolute path and needs nothing here.

# --- env-only overrides ---
# OLLAMA_BASE_URL=http://localhost:11434

# --- any setting, ad hoc ---
# Every Settings field can be overridden here with the SKUGGI_ prefix, e.g.:
# SKUGGI_PROVIDER=anthropic
# SKUGGI_ENGAGEMENT_ROOT=~/work/acme-2026   # the engagement directory (a path)
# Point at a different config file (default <config home>/config.json):
# SKUGGI_CONFIG_PATH=/path/to/config.json
# Relocate the homes themselves:
# SKUGGI_CONFIG_HOME=~/.config/skuggi
# SKUGGI_DATA_HOME=~/.local/share/skuggi
